# Golden files are compared byte-for-byte against strings that tests build with
# "\n". With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default, and what this repo is
# developed on) git rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, so the comparison fails
# on line endings alone while every line matches. That is what broke
# TestToFacts_EmittedPredicateArity_ShouldMatchGolden: 25 identical lines, 25
# CRLF pairs, one failing test.
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps golden files byte-stable on every platform.
#
# Note: .gitignore line 20 ignores all dotfiles ("(.*)"), which catches this
# file too, so it had to be added with "git add -f".
*.golden text eol=lf
